-- Canada Pension Plan Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-8), Part I, Divisions A and B (sections 5 to 20) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a worker, self-employed person, survivor, child or person with a disability who contributes to, or may claim from, the Canada
-- Pension Plan. This layer is the part of the seat that sections 5 to 20 answer: whether and how much the person must contribute,
-- what their employer must contribute in respect of them, what is counted as their earnings, and what they must do or tell the Minister.
-- The benefit questions are in the seat layers of the pieces that encode Parts II and III.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, dates and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the person
-- states, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked. The records the layer-1 modules expect are built inside each question,
-- in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is restated here. An optional fact (one that may
-- not have happened) is a yes/no answer and a date or amount. A record field that no rule called ever reads is given a fixed placeholder,
-- with a comment saying so.
--
-- WHAT THE PERSON CANNOT STATE. The rates are Schedule 1 and 2 figures, the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, the prescribed
-- exemption and the other regulation-set figures are asked as numbers: the Act sets them by Wage Measure data, schedules and regulations
-- that this encoding does not contain (NOTES.md, "Cross-references out of my ranges"). A substitution of any of them changes the answers.
-- Where the Minister must be satisfied of something (ss 11(3), 11(6)) the answer is conditional: "if the Minister is satisfied".
--
-- SIMPLIFICATIONS (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md, fork register): the excess-amount questions take up to two employments under the Plan and
-- one under a provincial pension plan; the self-employed earnings question takes up to two businesses; the pay of a year is asked month by month.
-- The layer-1 rules take any number.


§ `Canada Pension Plan -- Part I, Divisions A and B -- the individual's questions`

§§ `Sections 5 to 7 -- pensionable employment and excepted employment`

@export Which Minister does Part I (contributions) of the Plan name (s 5(1))?
GIVETH A Minister
DECIDE `Which Minister is the Minister for Part I of the Plan` IS
    `s 5(1) — the Minister for Part I`

@export Does an officer's act under Part I count as the Minister's act (s 5(2))?
GIVEN `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister authorized the officer who is dealing with you, or a class of officers that includes that officer, to exercise powers or perform duties of the Minister under Part I?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this officer's act under Part I count as an act of the Minister` IF
    `s 5(2) — an officer may exercise a power or perform a duty of the Minister under Part I` `the Minister has authorized the officer, or a class of officers that includes the officer, to act`

@export Is my employment pensionable employment (s 6(1))?
GIVEN `my employment is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in Canada?
      `my employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment under Her Majesty in right of Canada (the federal Crown)?
      `a regulation under section 7 includes my employment in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation made under section 7 include your employment in pensionable employment?
      `a regulation under section 7 excepts my employment from pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a regulation made under section 7 except your employment from pensionable employment?
      `my employment is in agriculture, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment in agriculture or an agricultural enterprise, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering (as regulation 2(2) defines those words)?
      `the cash remuneration my employer pays me in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How much cash remuneration does your employer pay you in the year, in dollars?
      `my employer employs me on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer employ you on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration?
      `the working days in the year for which my employer so employs me` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many working days in the year does your employer so employ you?
      `my employment is of a casual nature` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment of a casual nature?
      `my employment is for the purpose of my employer's trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your employment for the purpose of your employer's trade or business?
      `I am a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada?
      `I am employed by my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by your spouse or common-law partner?
      `my remuneration may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of my spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc May the remuneration paid to you be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of your spouse or common-law partner?
      `I am a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty?
      `my remuneration is paid either directly or by me to the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your remuneration paid either directly, or by you, to the order?
      `no cash remuneration is paid to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no cash remuneration paid to you?
      `I am the child of my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the child of your employer?
      `I am maintained by my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you maintained by your employer?
      `I am employed as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police?
      `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another Act of Parliament provide otherwise for your employment as a member of the Forces or the Police?
      `my employer employs persons in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your employer employ persons in Canada?
      `a reciprocal agreement exempts my employer from the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a reciprocal agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of another country exempt your employer from liability to make the contributions imposed on an employer by the Act?
      `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by Her Majesty in right of a province, or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province?
      `my employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you employed by the government of a country other than Canada, or by an international organization (as regulation 2(2) defines it)?
      `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in the Indian Act?
      `my earnings from the employment are not included in computing my income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your earnings from the employment left out of your income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my employment pensionable employment` IF
    `s 6(1) — the employment is pensionable employment` `my employment`
    WHERE
        `my employment` MEANS `cp1 Facts about an employment` WITH
            `the employment is in Canada` IS `my employment is in Canada`
            `the employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS `my employment is under Her Majesty in right of Canada`
            `a regulation made under section 7 includes the employment in pensionable employment` IS `a regulation under section 7 includes my employment in pensionable employment`
            `a regulation made under section 7 excepts the employment from pensionable employment` IS `a regulation under section 7 excepts my employment from pensionable employment`
            `the employment is in agriculture or an agricultural enterprise, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering` IS `my employment is in agriculture, horticulture, fishing, hunting, trapping, forestry, logging or lumbering`
            `cash remuneration the employer pays the employee in the year` IS `the cash remuneration my employer pays me in the year`
            `the employer employs the employee on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration` IS `my employer employs me on terms providing for payment of cash remuneration`
            `working days in the year for which the employer so employs the employee` IS `the working days in the year for which my employer so employs me`
            `the employment is of a casual nature` IS `my employment is of a casual nature`
            `the employment is for the purpose of the employer's trade or business` IS `my employment is for the purpose of my employer's trade or business`
            `the employee is a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada` IS `I am a teacher on exchange from a country other than Canada`
            `the employee is employed by the employee's spouse or common-law partner` IS `I am employed by my spouse or common-law partner`
            `the remuneration paid may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of the spouse or common-law partner` IS `my remuneration may be deducted under the Income Tax Act in computing the income of my spouse or common-law partner`
            `the employee is a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty` IS `I am a member of a religious order who has taken a vow of perpetual poverty`
            `the remuneration is paid either directly or by the member to the order` IS `my remuneration is paid either directly or by me to the order`
            `no cash remuneration is paid` IS `no cash remuneration is paid to me`
            `the employee is the child of the employer` IS `I am the child of my employer`
            `the employee is maintained by the employer` IS `I am maintained by my employer`
            `the employment is as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police` IS `I am employed as a member of the Canadian Forces or the Royal Canadian Mounted Police`
            `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for that employment` IS `another Act of Parliament provides otherwise for my employment`
            `the employer employs persons in Canada` IS `my employer employs persons in Canada`
            `a reciprocal agreement between the Government of Canada and the government of another country exempts the employer from liability to make the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act` IS `a reciprocal agreement exempts my employer from the contributions imposed on an employer by this Act`
            `the employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province` IS `my employment is by Her Majesty in right of a province or by an agent of Her Majesty in right of a province`
            `the employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization` IS `my employment is by the government of a country other than Canada or by an international organization`
            `the employee is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act`
            `the earnings from the employment are not included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS `my earnings from the employment are not included in computing my income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act`

