            `the earnings from the employment are not included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act` IS `my earnings from the employment are not included in computing my income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act`

@export Can a regulation make my employer, a foreign government or an international organization, pay an employer's contribution (s 7(4))?
GIVEN `a regulation requires an employer's contribution from the government of a country other than Canada or from an international organization` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the regulation require the payment of an employer's contribution by the government of a country other than Canada, or by an international organization, that employs you?
      `the regulation is made pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the regulation made pursuant to an agreement with the employing government or organization referred to in paragraph 7(1)(f)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can a regulation make my foreign government or international organization employer pay an employer's contribution` IF
    `s 7(4) — a regulation under section 7 may require an employer's contribution from a foreign government or an international organization` `a regulation requires an employer's contribution from the government of a country other than Canada or from an international organization` `the regulation is made pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 7(1)(f)`

§§ `Section 8 -- what I must contribute as an employee`

-- s 8(1). The employee makes the contribution by deduction from remuneration. Rate times the lesser of (a) the salary and wages less the prescribed exemption
-- and (b) the maximum contributory earnings less any base contribution already made on the pay under a provincial pension plan.
@export How much must I contribute for the year as my base contribution as an employee, in dollars (s 8(1))?
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer, in dollars? (Section 12 works them out; see the question on your contributory salary and wages.)
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount has been prescribed by regulation as or on account of your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 16: your maximum pensionable earnings less your basic exemption.)
      `part of my pay from this employer was already counted for a base contribution under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of your salary and wages paid by this employer already been counted for a base contribution that you made under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which that base contribution was made under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much of your salary and wages was that, in dollars (as determined in the prescribed manner)? (Zero if not.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute as an employee for the year as my base contribution` IS
    `s 8(1) — the employee's base contribution for the year` `the contribution rate for employees for the year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` (IF `part of my pay from this employer was already counted for a base contribution under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which that base contribution was made under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 8(1.1). For 2019 and each subsequent year. NOTHING: no first additional contribution is imposed for an earlier year.
@export How much must I contribute for the year as my first additional contribution as an employee, in dollars (s 8(1.1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer, in dollars? (Section 12 works them out; see the question on your contributory salary and wages.)
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount has been prescribed by regulation as or on account of your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 16: your maximum pensionable earnings less your basic exemption.)
      `part of my pay from this employer was already counted for a first additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of your salary and wages paid by this employer already been counted for a first additional contribution that you made under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which that first additional contribution was made under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much of your salary and wages was that, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute as an employee for the year as my first additional contribution` IS
    `s 8(1.1) — the employee's first additional contribution for the year` `the year I am asking about` `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` (IF `part of my pay from this employer was already counted for a first additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which that first additional contribution was made under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 8(1.2). For 2024 and each subsequent year. NOTHING: no second additional contribution is imposed for an earlier year.
@export How much must I contribute for the year as my second additional contribution as an employee, in dollars (s 8(1.2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer, in dollars? (Section 12 works them out; see the question on your contributory salary and wages.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `part of my pay from this employer was already counted for a second additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of your salary and wages paid by this employer already been counted for a second additional contribution that you made under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which that second additional contribution was made under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much of your salary and wages was that, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute as an employee for the year as my second additional contribution` IS
    `s 8(1.2) — the employee's second additional contribution for the year` `the year I am asking about` `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` (IF `part of my pay from this employer was already counted for a second additional contribution under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which that second additional contribution was made under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 8(2) and (3), with the prorating of s 8(4) to (11). Up to two employments under the Plan and one under a provincial pension plan; a figure of zero is no pay.
-- The figures "leaving out paragraphs (b) and (c)" are the ones subsections 8(6), (7), (10) and (11) ask for.
@export Has too much been deducted from my pay for the year under the Plan and a provincial pension plan (s 8(2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year from your first employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your second employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your employment to which a provincial pension plan applies (for example in Quebec), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also an individual with self-employed earnings to whom section 10 and the contribution provisions apply?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees for the year under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction? (Zero if none.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the first additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the second additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year if paragraphs 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are they if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your contributions under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your contributions under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has an excess amount been deducted from my pay for the year` IS
    `s 8(2) — an excess amount has been paid` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my first employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my second employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my provincial employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `my first employment`, `my second employment`, `my provincial employment`
            `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS (IF `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` THEN JUST `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS `my basic exemption for the year`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan`

-- s 8(2) and (3), with the prorating of s 8(4) to (11). Up to two employments under the Plan and one under a provincial pension plan; a figure of zero is no pay.
-- The figures "leaving out paragraphs (b) and (c)" are the ones subsections 8(6), (7), (10) and (11) ask for.
@export By how much has too much been deducted from my pay for the year, in dollars (s 8(2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year from your first employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your second employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your employment to which a provincial pension plan applies (for example in Quebec), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also an individual with self-employed earnings to whom section 10 and the contribution provisions apply?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees for the year under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction? (Zero if none.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the first additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the second additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year if paragraphs 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are they if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your contributions under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your contributions under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `By how much has too much been deducted from my pay for the year` IS
    `s 8(2) — the excess amount calculated` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my first employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my second employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my provincial employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `my first employment`, `my second employment`, `my provincial employment`
            `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS (IF `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` THEN JUST `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS `my basic exemption for the year`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan`

-- s 8(2) and (3), with the prorating of s 8(4) to (11). Up to two employments under the Plan and one under a provincial pension plan; a figure of zero is no pay.
-- The figures "leaving out paragraphs (b) and (c)" are the ones subsections 8(6), (7), (10) and (11) ask for.
@export How much of what was deducted is my overpayment under the Plan, in dollars (s 8(3))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year from your first employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your second employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your employment to which a provincial pension plan applies (for example in Quebec), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also an individual with self-employed earnings to whom section 10 and the contribution provisions apply?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees for the year under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction? (Zero if none.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the first additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the second additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year if paragraphs 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are they if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your contributions under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your contributions under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is my overpayment of contributions under the Plan for the year` IS
    `s 8(3) — the overpayment made by the employee on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my first employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my second employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my provincial employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `my first employment`, `my second employment`, `my provincial employment`
            `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS (IF `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` THEN JUST `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS `my basic exemption for the year`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan`

§§ `Section 9 -- what my employer must contribute in respect of me`

-- Situational: the questions on a new employer (s 9(2)) and on a corporation you control (s 9(3)) only arise if your employer changed or you used to be self-employed. Ask first: "Has this happened to you?"

-- s 9(1). The correlative of s 8(1): the employer makes a contribution in respect of each employee in pensionable employment.
@export What base contribution must my employer make in respect of me for the year, in dollars (s 9(1))?
GIVEN `the contribution rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employers for the year, as a fraction? (Schedule 1.)
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer, in dollars? (Section 12 works them out; see the question on your contributory salary and wages.)
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount has been prescribed as or on account of your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 16: your maximum pensionable earnings less your basic exemption.)
      `part of my pay was already counted for a base contribution by my employer under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of your salary and wages already been counted for a base contribution that your employer made in respect of you under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which that base contribution was made by my employer under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What base contribution must my employer make in respect of me for the year` IS
    `s 9(1) — the employer's base contribution for the year in respect of an employee` `the contribution rate for employers for the year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` (IF `part of my pay was already counted for a base contribution by my employer under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which that base contribution was made by my employer under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 9(1.1). For 2019 and each subsequent year.
@export What first additional contribution must my employer make in respect of me for the year, in dollars (s 9(1.1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year, as a fraction? (Schedule 2.)
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer, in dollars? (Section 12 works them out; see the question on your contributory salary and wages.)
      `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount has been prescribed as or on account of your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 16: your maximum pensionable earnings less your basic exemption.)
      `part of my pay was already counted for a first additional contribution by my employer under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of your salary and wages already been counted for a first additional contribution that your employer made in respect of you under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which that first additional contribution was made by my employer under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What first additional contribution must my employer make in respect of me for the year` IS
    `s 9(1.1) — the employer's first additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` `the year I am asking about` `the first additional contribution rate for employers for the year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` `the amount prescribed as or on account of my basic exemption for the year` `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` (IF `part of my pay was already counted for a first additional contribution by my employer under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which that first additional contribution was made by my employer under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 9(1.2). For 2024 and each subsequent year.
@export What second additional contribution must my employer make in respect of me for the year, in dollars (s 9(1.2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year, as a fraction? (Schedule 2.)
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer, in dollars? (Section 12 works them out; see the question on your contributory salary and wages.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `part of my pay was already counted for a second additional contribution by my employer under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has any of your salary and wages already been counted for a second additional contribution that your employer made in respect of you under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which that second additional contribution was made by my employer under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What second additional contribution must my employer make in respect of me for the year` IS
    `s 9(1.2) — the employer's second additional contribution for the year in respect of an employee` `the year I am asking about` `the second additional contribution rate for employers for the year` `my contributory salary and wages for the year paid by this employer` `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` (IF `part of my pay was already counted for a second additional contribution by my employer under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which that second additional contribution was made by my employer under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

@export May my new employer count what my former employer paid, deducted, remitted or contributed for me this year (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `my new employer immediately succeeds my former employer as my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your new employer immediately succeed your former employer as your employer?
      `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the succession a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation?
      `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of my former employer's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the succession a result of the acquisition of all or part of your former employer's business?
      `the acquisition is with the agreement of my former employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acquisition with the agreement of the former employer?
      `the acquisition is by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acquisition by operation of law?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my new employer count what my former employer paid for me this year` IF
    `s 9(2) — the successor employer may take into account the amounts the former employer paid, deducted, remitted or contributed` `my new employer immediately succeeds my former employer as my employer` `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation` `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of my former employer's business` `the acquisition is with the agreement of my former employer` `the acquisition is by operation of law`

@export How much may my new employer count as if it had paid, deducted, remitted or contributed it (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `my new employer immediately succeeds my former employer as my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your new employer immediately succeed your former employer as your employer?
      `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the succession a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation?
      `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of my former employer's business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the succession a result of the acquisition of all or part of your former employer's business?
      `the acquisition is with the agreement of my former employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acquisition with the agreement of the former employer?
      `the acquisition is by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the acquisition by operation of law?
      `what my former employer paid, deducted, remitted or contributed under the Plan for the year in relation to my employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What did your former employer pay, deduct, remit or contribute under the Plan in respect of the year in relation to your employment, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may my new employer count of what my former employer paid for me this year` IS
    `s 9(2) — the amount the successor employer may take into account as if it had paid, deducted, remitted or contributed it` (`s 9(2) — the successor employer may take into account the amounts the former employer paid, deducted, remitted or contributed` `my new employer immediately succeeds my former employer as my employer` `the succession is a result of the formation or dissolution of a corporation` `the succession is a result of the acquisition of all or part of my former employer's business` `the acquisition is with the agreement of my former employer` `the acquisition is by operation of law`) `what my former employer paid, deducted, remitted or contributed under the Plan for the year in relation to my employment`

@export Must my new employer also take those amounts into account for the contributions deducted from my pay (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `my new employer takes those amounts into account for its own contributions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your new employer take those amounts into account with respect to the employer's contributions?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my new employer also take those amounts into account for the contributions deducted from my pay` IF
    `s 9(2) — the successor employer must also take the amounts into account with respect to the employee's contributions` `my new employer takes those amounts into account for its own contributions`

@export May the corporation I control count my earlier self-employment (s 9(3))?
GIVEN `in the year I was self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you self-employed in the year?
      `I ceased to be self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be self-employed?
      `I became an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become an employee of a corporation that you control?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the corporation I control count my earlier self-employment` IF
    `s 9(3) — the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `in the year I was self-employed` `I ceased to be self-employed` `I became an employee of a corporation that I control`

@export How much of my self-employed earnings may the corporation count as salary and wages it paid me (s 9(3)(a))?
GIVEN `in the year I was self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you self-employed in the year?
      `I ceased to be self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be self-employed?
      `I became an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become an employee of a corporation that you control?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What were your contributory self-employed earnings in the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my self-employed earnings may the corporation I control count as salary and wages it paid me` IS
    `s 9(3)(a) — the amount the corporation may take into account as contributory salary and wages paid to the employee in that year` (`s 9(3) — the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `in the year I was self-employed` `I ceased to be self-employed` `I became an employee of a corporation that I control`) `my contributory self-employed earnings in the year`

-- One half of the contributions (NOTES.md, fork register: "one half of that amount").
@export How much of my self-employed contributions may the corporation count as deducted from my pay (s 9(3)(b))?
GIVEN `in the year I was self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you self-employed in the year?
      `I ceased to be self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be self-employed?
      `I became an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become an employee of a corporation that you control?
      `my contributions in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What contributions did you make in respect of your self-employed earnings in the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my self-employed contributions may the corporation I control count as employee contributions` IS
    `s 9(3)(b) — the amount the corporation may take into account in relation to the employee's contributions for that year` (`s 9(3) — the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `in the year I was self-employed` `I ceased to be self-employed` `I became an employee of a corporation that I control`) `my contributions in respect of self-employed earnings in the year`

-- One half of the contributions (NOTES.md, fork register: "one half of that amount").
@export How much of my self-employed contributions may the corporation count as contributed by the employer (s 9(3)(b))?
GIVEN `in the year I was self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you self-employed in the year?
      `I ceased to be self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be self-employed?
      `I became an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become an employee of a corporation that you control?
      `my contributions in respect of self-employed earnings in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What contributions did you make in respect of your self-employed earnings in the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my self-employed contributions may the corporation I control count as employer contributions` IS
    `s 9(3)(b) — the amount the corporation may take into account in relation to the employer's contributions for that year` (`s 9(3) — the corporation may take into account the person's self-employment` `in the year I was self-employed` `I ceased to be self-employed` `I became an employee of a corporation that I control`) `my contributions in respect of self-employed earnings in the year`

§§ `Section 10 -- what I must contribute on my self-employed earnings`

-- Situational: the questions on s 10(2) only arise if you have moved from employment by a corporation you control to self-employment. Ask first: "Has this happened to you?"

-- s 10(1). NOTHING: section 10 imposes nothing (not resident in Canada, or no contributory self-employed earnings).
@export How much must I contribute on my self-employed earnings for the year as my base contribution, in dollars (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 13.)
      `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.099)? (Schedule 1.)
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of your basic exemption for the year by your employers, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of a like exemption for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of a like exemption under a provincial pension plan, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 16: your maximum pensionable earnings less your basic exemption.)
      `I have salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year?
      `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars? (Section 15.)
      `I have salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have salary and wages on which you made a base contribution for the year under a provincial pension plan?
      `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars (as determined in the prescribed manner)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute on my self-employed earnings for the year as my base contribution` IS
    `s 10(1) — the individual's base contribution on self-employed earnings for the year` `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `my basic exemption for the year` `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers` `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of a like exemption for the year under a provincial pension plan` `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` (IF `I have salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` THEN JUST `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I have salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 10(1.1). For 2019 and each subsequent year, for an individual referred to in subsection (1).
@export How much must I contribute on my self-employed earnings for the year as my first additional contribution, in dollars (s 10(1.1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 13.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a fraction? (Schedule 2.)
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of your basic exemption for the year by your employers, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of a like exemption for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of a like exemption under a provincial pension plan, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 16: your maximum pensionable earnings less your basic exemption.)
      `I have salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year?
      `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars? (Section 15.1.)
      `I have salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have salary and wages on which you made a first additional contribution for the year under a provincial pension plan?
      `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute on my self-employed earnings for the year as my first additional contribution` IS
    `s 10(1.1) — the individual's first additional contribution on self-employed earnings for the year` `the year I am asking about` `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `my basic exemption for the year` `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers` `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of a like exemption for the year under a provincial pension plan` `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` (IF `I have salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` THEN JUST `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I have salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 10(1.2). For 2024 and each subsequent year, for an individual referred to in subsection (1).
@export How much must I contribute on my self-employed earnings for the year as my second additional contribution, in dollars (s 10(1.2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 13.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, as a fraction? (Schedule 2.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `I have salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year?
      `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars? (Section 15.2.)
      `I have salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have salary and wages on which you made a second additional contribution for the year under a provincial pension plan?
      `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how much, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much must I contribute on my self-employed earnings for the year as my second additional contribution` IS
    `s 10(1.2) — the individual's second additional contribution on self-employed earnings for the year` `the year I am asking about` `I am resident in Canada for the purposes of the Income Tax Act during the year` `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` (IF `I have salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` THEN JUST `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `I have salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` THEN JUST `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING)

@export May I count the payments of the corporation I controlled when I become self-employed (s 10(2))?
GIVEN `in the year I was an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, in the year, an employee of a corporation that you control?
      `I ceased to be employed by that corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be employed by that corporation?
      `I became self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become self-employed?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I count the payments of the corporation I controlled when I become self-employed` IF
    `s 10(2) — the person may take into account the corporation's payments` `in the year I was an employee of a corporation that I control` `I ceased to be employed by that corporation` `I became self-employed`

@export How much may I count as contributory self-employed earnings from the corporation's salary and wages (s 10(2)(a))?
GIVEN `in the year I was an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, in the year, an employee of a corporation that you control?
      `I ceased to be employed by that corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be employed by that corporation?
      `I became self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become self-employed?
      `the contributory salary and wages the corporation paid me in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What contributory salary and wages did the corporation pay you in the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may I count as self-employed earnings from the salary and wages my corporation paid me` IS
    `s 10(2)(a) — the amount the person may take into account as contributory self-employed earnings in the year` (`s 10(2) — the person may take into account the corporation's payments` `in the year I was an employee of a corporation that I control` `I ceased to be employed by that corporation` `I became self-employed`) `the contributory salary and wages the corporation paid me in the year`

@export How much may I count as my own contributions from what the corporation deducted and contributed (s 10(2)(b))?
GIVEN `in the year I was an employee of a corporation that I control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you, in the year, an employee of a corporation that you control?
      `I ceased to be employed by that corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you cease to be employed by that corporation?
      `I became self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you become self-employed?
      `the amounts the corporation deducted, remitted or contributed in relation to my contributions as an employee for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What amounts did the corporation deduct, remit or contribute in relation to your contributions as an employee for the year, in dollars?
      `the amounts the corporation deducted, remitted or contributed in relation to the employer's contributions in respect of me for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc And in relation to the employer's contributions in respect of you for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much may I count as my own contributions from what my corporation deducted and contributed` IS
    `s 10(2)(b) — the amount the person may take into account as contributions by the person in respect of self-employment earnings in that year` (`s 10(2) — the person may take into account the corporation's payments` `in the year I was an employee of a corporation that I control` `I ceased to be employed by that corporation` `I became self-employed`) `the amounts the corporation deducted, remitted or contributed in relation to my contributions as an employee for the year` `the amounts the corporation deducted, remitted or contributed in relation to the employer's contributions in respect of me for the year`

§§ `Section 11 -- the election not to contribute on self-employed earnings (members of certain religious sects)`

-- Situational: this group only arises if you are a member of a religious sect that the Minister has certified (or may certify). Ask first: "Are you a member of such a sect?"

-- s 11(1), subject to (2) and (5). The election has effect from January 1 of the year it is filed, if approved, to the year the Minister receives a revocation.
@export Is section 10 not applying to me for the year because of my election (s 11(1), (2) and (5))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `I am a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect certified by the Minister under subsection 11(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a member of a religious sect, or a division of one, that the Minister has certified under subsection 11(6)?
      `I elect not to make a contribution with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect not to make a contribution with respect to the year?
      `my election is made in the prescribed manner and form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your election in the manner and form prescribed?
      `the Minister has approved my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved your election?
      `the year in which I filed my election with the Minister` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did you file your election with the Minister?
      `the Minister has received a revocation of my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received a revocation of your election?
      `the year in which the Minister received the revocation` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, in what year? (Any year if not.)
      `I made this election after revoking an earlier election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make this election after revoking an earlier election under section 11?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 10 not apply to me for the year because of my election` IF
    `s 11(1) — section 10 does not apply with respect to the year to the individual` `I am a member of a religious sect or a division of a religious sect certified by the Minister under subsection 11(6)` `I elect not to make a contribution with respect to the year` (`s 11(2) — the election has effect for a year` `the year I am asking about` `my election is made in the prescribed manner and form` `the Minister has approved my election` `the year in which I filed my election with the Minister` (IF `the Minister has received a revocation of my election` THEN JUST `the year in which the Minister received the revocation` ELSE NOTHING)) (`s 11(5) — the individual may make an election under section 11 with respect to a subsequent year` `I made this election after revoking an earlier election`)

-- s 11(3). The Minister approves where the Minister is satisfied; the answer is conditional on that judgment, which only the Minister makes.
@export Must the Minister approve my election, if satisfied of these matters (s 11(3))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that I am a member of a religious sect or a division of one certified under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that you are a member of a religious sect, or a division of one, certified under subsection (6)?
      `the Minister is satisfied that a spokesman for the sect or division has certified me as a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that a spokesman for the sect or division has certified you as a member?
      `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the spokesman has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as being members?
      `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has certified that the sect or division maintains the tenets, teachings and practices of subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the spokesman has certified that the sect or division maintains tenets, teachings and practices of the kinds in subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister approve my election if satisfied of these matters` IF
    `s 11(3) — the Minister must approve the election` `the Minister is satisfied that I am a member of a religious sect or a division of one certified under subsection (6)` `the Minister is satisfied that a spokesman for the sect or division has certified me as a member` `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has been authorized by the sect or division to certify persons as members` `the Minister is satisfied that the spokesman has certified that the sect or division maintains the tenets, teachings and practices of subparagraphs (6)(a)(i) and (ii)`

-- s 11(6). Conditional on the Minister being satisfied and on the sect having applied.
@export Must the Minister certify my religious sect, if satisfied of these matters (s 11(6))?
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that my sect is a religious organization with established tenets and teachings opposing the acceptance of benefits from private or public insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the sect is a religious organization that has established tenets and teachings that oppose the acceptance of benefits from any private or public insurance that provides for payments in the event of death, disability, old age or retirement?
      `the Minister is satisfied that my sect makes reasonable provision for the support of dependent members` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the sect does, as a practice, make provisions for the support of dependent members that are reasonable in view of their general level of living?
      `the Minister is satisfied that my sect existed in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has kept those tenets and practices since` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Minister satisfied that the sect was in existence in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has been maintaining those tenets, teachings and practices since that date?
      `my sect or division has applied to the Minister in prescribed form for certification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the sect or division applied to the Minister in prescribed form for certification?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister certify my religious sect if satisfied of these matters` IF
    `s 11(6) — the Minister must certify the religious sect or division` `the Minister is satisfied that my sect is a religious organization with established tenets and teachings opposing the acceptance of benefits from private or public insurance` `the Minister is satisfied that my sect makes reasonable provision for the support of dependent members` `the Minister is satisfied that my sect existed in Canada on January 1, 1966 and has kept those tenets and practices since` `my sect or division has applied to the Minister in prescribed form for certification`

@export Must the Minister return a contribution I made for a year I elected not to contribute (s 11(4))?
GIVEN `I made a contribution with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a contribution with respect to the year?
      `I elect under section 11 not to make a contribution with respect to the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you elect under section 11 not to make a contribution with respect to that year?
      `I have applied for the return of the contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the return of the contribution?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the contribution I made be returned to me` IF
    `s 11(4) — the contribution must be returned to the contributor` `I made a contribution with respect to the year` `I elect under section 11 not to make a contribution with respect to the year` `I have applied for the return of the contribution`

@export May I make a new election under section 11 after revoking one (s 11(5))?
GIVEN `I have elected not to make a contribution for a year and have revoked that election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you elected not to make a contribution with respect to a year and then revoked the election?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make a new election under section 11 after revoking one` IF
    `s 11(5) — the individual may make an election under section 11 with respect to a subsequent year` `I have elected not to make a contribution for a year and have revoked that election`

@export In what year does my approved election begin to have effect (s 11(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the Minister has approved my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister approved your election?
      `the year in which I filed my election with the Minister` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did you file your election with the Minister?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `In what year does my election begin to have effect` IS
    `s 11(2)(b) — the first year for which the election has effect` `the Minister has approved my election` `the year in which I filed my election with the Minister`

-- The election ceases on January 1 of the year after the Minister receives the revocation, so its last year is the year of receipt. NOTHING: not revoked.
@export In what year does my election cease to have effect (s 11(2)(c))?
GIVEN `the Minister has received a revocation of my election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Minister received a revocation of your election?
      `the year in which the Minister received the revocation` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, in what year? (Any year if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `In what year does my election cease to have effect` IS
    `s 11(2)(c) — the last year for which the election has effect` (IF `the Minister has received a revocation of my election` THEN JUST `the year in which the Minister received the revocation` ELSE NOTHING)

§§ `Sections 11.1 and 11.2 -- the contribution rates`

-- s 11.1. The Act states the rate for 1966 to 1986 (1.8% for employees and employers, 3.6% for the self-employed); from 1987 the rate is the one Schedule 1 sets. NOTHING: before 1966.
@export What contribution rate applies to me for the year (s 11.1)?
GIVEN `I contribute as` IS A `Contributing capacity` @desc Do you contribute as an employee, as an employer or as a self-employed person? (One of: contributing as an employee, contributing as an employer, contributing as a self-employed person.)
      `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the rate Schedule 1 sets for me for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What rate does Schedule 1 set for you for the year, as a fraction? (Needed from 1987; any number before.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What contribution rate applies to me for the year` IS
    `s 11.1 — the contribution rate for a capacity and a year` `I contribute as` `the year I am asking about` `the rate Schedule 1 sets for me for the year`

-- s 11.2. From 2019, the rates Schedule 2 sets. NOTHING: the base tier, or an earlier year.
@export What first or second additional contribution rate applies to me for the year (s 11.2)?
GIVEN `the contribution I am asking about is` IS A Tier @desc Which contribution are you asking about? (One of: the base tier, the first additional tier, the second additional tier.)
      `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the rate Schedule 2 sets for me for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What rate does Schedule 2 set for you for the year, as a fraction?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What first or second additional contribution rate applies to me for the year` IS
    `s 11.2 — the first or second additional contribution rate for a tier and a year` `the contribution I am asking about is` `the year I am asking about` `the rate Schedule 2 sets for me for the year`

§§ `Section 12 -- my contributory salary and wages`

-- s 12(1). Left out: income received (a) before you reach 18, (b) in a month excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability, (c) after 65 while a retirement pension is payable
-- and an election to exclude it has effect, and (d) after you reach 70. You reach an age on the first day of the month after your birthday (s 2(2)).
@export Is the pay I received on a date left out of my contributory salary and wages (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your contributory period under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, end by reason of disability during the year?
      `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a disability pension payable to you under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, stop being payable during the year?
      `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any months excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
      `the first month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that run of excluded months ended?
      `the last month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If it has ended, what is the last month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `a retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to you under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month for which it is payable? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) to exclude your income after you reach sixty-five years of age?
      `the date I made that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you make it? (Any date if not.)
      `I have revoked that election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election?
      `the date I revoked that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) to exclude your self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does it refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election to exclude self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my revocation` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does the revocation refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `the date I received the pay` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the pay you are asking about?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the pay I received on a date left out of my contributory salary and wages` IF
    `s 12(1) — income received on a date is not included in the contributory salary and wages` `my facts` `the date I received the pay`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about a person for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `date of birth of the person` IS `my date of birth`
            -- Placeholder: the rules this question calls do not read the date of death.
            `date of death of the person` IS NOTHING
            `date the contributory period of the person ends by reason of disability` IS (IF `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` THEN JUST `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the disability pension ceases to be payable to the person` IS (IF `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` THEN JUST `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `months excluded from the contributory period of the person by reason of disability` IS
                IF `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` THEN LIST `my run of excluded months` ELSE EMPTY
            `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person` IS (IF `a retirement pension is payable to me` THEN JUST `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` THEN JUST `the date I made that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have revoked that election` THEN JUST `the date I revoked that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)` IS (IF `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my revocation` ELSE NOTHING)
        `my run of excluded months` MEANS `cp1 Month period` WITH
            `first month of the month period` IS `the first month excluded by reason of disability`
            `last month of the month period` IS (IF `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` THEN JUST `the last month excluded by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 12(1). Your income for the year from pensionable employment, as the Income Tax Act computes it (month by month here), plus the deductions, less the income the subsection leaves out.
@export What are my contributory salary and wages for the year from pensionable employment, before subsections (2) to (3), in dollars (s 12(1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your contributory period under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, end by reason of disability during the year?
      `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a disability pension payable to you under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, stop being payable during the year?
      `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any months excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
      `the first month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that run of excluded months ended?
      `the last month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If it has ended, what is the last month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `a retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to you under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month for which it is payable? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) to exclude your income after you reach sixty-five years of age?
      `the date I made that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you make it? (Any date if not.)
      `I have revoked that election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election?
      `the date I revoked that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) to exclude your self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does it refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election to exclude self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my revocation` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does the revocation refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `my pay received in January` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in January of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in February` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in February of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in March` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in March of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in April` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in April of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in May` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in May of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in June` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in June of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in July` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in July of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in August` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in August of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in September` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in September of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in October` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in October of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in November` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in November of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my pay received in December` IS A NUMBER @desc How much pay from this employment did you receive in December of the year, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `the deductions made in computing my income from that employment, other than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What deductions for the year were made in computing your income from pensionable employment, other than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of the Income Tax Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my contributory salary and wages for the year from pensionable employment` IS
    `s 12(1) — the contributory salary and wages of a person for a year` `my facts` `my receipts` `the deductions made in computing my income from that employment, other than under paragraph 8(1)(c) of the Income Tax Act`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about a person for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `date of birth of the person` IS `my date of birth`
            -- Placeholder: the rules this question calls do not read the date of death.
            `date of death of the person` IS NOTHING
            `date the contributory period of the person ends by reason of disability` IS (IF `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` THEN JUST `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the disability pension ceases to be payable to the person` IS (IF `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` THEN JUST `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `months excluded from the contributory period of the person by reason of disability` IS
                IF `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` THEN LIST `my run of excluded months` ELSE EMPTY
            `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person` IS (IF `a retirement pension is payable to me` THEN JUST `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` THEN JUST `the date I made that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have revoked that election` THEN JUST `the date I revoked that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)` IS (IF `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my revocation` ELSE NOTHING)
        `my run of excluded months` MEANS `cp1 Month period` WITH
            `first month of the month period` IS `the first month excluded by reason of disability`
            `last month of the month period` IS (IF `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` THEN JUST `the last month excluded by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)
        -- Every boundary in subsection 12(1) falls on the first day of a month, so a payment is dated the first day of the month it was received in.
        `my pay received in January, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 1 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in January`
        `my pay received in February, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 2 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in February`
        `my pay received in March, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 3 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in March`
        `my pay received in April, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 4 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in April`
        `my pay received in May, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 5 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in May`
        `my pay received in June, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 6 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in June`
        `my pay received in July, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 7 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in July`
        `my pay received in August, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 8 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in August`
        `my pay received in September, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 9 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in September`
        `my pay received in October, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 10 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in October`
        `my pay received in November, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 11 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in November`
        `my pay received in December, as a receipt` MEANS `cp1 Income receipt` WITH
            `date the income is received` IS YearMonthDay `the year I am asking about` 12 1
            `amount of the income received` IS `my pay received in December`
        `my receipts` MEANS LIST `my pay received in January, as a receipt`, `my pay received in February, as a receipt`, `my pay received in March, as a receipt`, `my pay received in April, as a receipt`, `my pay received in May, as a receipt`, `my pay received in June, as a receipt`, `my pay received in July, as a receipt`, `my pay received in August, as a receipt`, `my pay received in September, as a receipt`, `my pay received in October, as a receipt`, `my pay received in November, as a receipt`, `my pay received in December, as a receipt`

@export Is a public servant's salary included in my contributory salary and wages (s 12(2))?
GIVEN `I am a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act?
      `my salary, as that Act defines it, not otherwise included in my income for the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your salary, as the Public Service Superannuation Act defines it, that is not otherwise included in your income for the Income Tax Act, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my public service salary is included in my contributory salary and wages` IS
    `s 12(2) — the salary of a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act included in the contributory salary and wages` `I am a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act` `my salary, as that Act defines it, not otherwise included in my income for the Income Tax Act`

@export Is an Indian's income from otherwise excepted employment included in my contributory salary and wages (s 12(2.1))?
GIVEN `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in the Indian Act?
      `my income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations provide to be included` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) do the regulations made under subsection 7(1) provide to be included, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my income as an Indian from otherwise excepted employment is included in my contributory salary and wages` IS
    `s 12(2.1) — the income of an Indian from employment otherwise excepted that is included in the contributory salary and wages` `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` `my income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations provide to be included`

@export What are my contributory salary and wages for the year, with subsections (2), (2.1) and (3) applied, in dollars (s 12)?
GIVEN `my contributory salary and wages as subsection 12(1) works them out` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages as subsection 12(1) works them out, in dollars? (The question above gives them.)
      `I am a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act?
      `my salary, as that Act defines it, not otherwise included in my income for the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your salary, as the Public Service Superannuation Act defines it, that is not otherwise included in your income for the Income Tax Act, in dollars?
      `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in the Indian Act?
      `my income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations provide to be included` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) do the regulations made under subsection 7(1) provide to be included, in dollars?
      `my remuneration is paid in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your remuneration paid in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan?
      `my income for the year from that employment as the provincial pension plan requires it to be computed` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the year from that employment as the provincial pension plan requires it to be computed, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my contributory salary and wages for the year with the public service, Indian and provincial rules applied` IS
    `s 12(3) — the contributory salary and wages for remuneration paid in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `my remuneration is paid in respect of pensionable employment in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `my income for the year from that employment as the provincial pension plan requires it to be computed` (`s 12 — the contributory salary and wages of a person for a year, with the inclusions of subsections (2) and (2.1)` `my contributory salary and wages as subsection 12(1) works them out` (`s 12(2) — the salary of a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act included in the contributory salary and wages` `I am a contributor under the Public Service Superannuation Act` `my salary, as that Act defines it, not otherwise included in my income for the Income Tax Act`) (`s 12(2.1) — the income of an Indian from employment otherwise excepted that is included in the contributory salary and wages` `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` `my income from employment otherwise excepted under paragraph 6(2)(j.1) that the regulations provide to be included`))

-- s 12(1.1): in the prescribed form and manner (a), only once in a year (d), and not in a year in which an election is revoked (f).
@export May I make an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five (s 12(1.1)(a), (d) and (f))?
GIVEN `my election or revocation is made in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your election, or your revocation of it, made in the prescribed form and manner?
      `I have already made an election in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already made an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) in the year?
      `an election of mine is revoked in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an election of yours under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) revoked in the year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` IF
    `s 12(1.1) — a valid election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) may be made` `my election or revocation is made in the prescribed form and manner` `I have already made an election in the year` `an election of mine is revoked in the year`

-- s 12(1.1): in the prescribed form and manner (a), and not in the year the election was made (e).
@export May I revoke my election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five (s 12(1.1)(a) and (e))?
GIVEN `my election or revocation is made in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your election, or your revocation of it, made in the prescribed form and manner?
      `the year in which I made the election` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did you make the election?
      `the year in which I revoke the election` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year do you revoke it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I revoke my election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` IF
    `s 12(1.1) — a valid revocation of the election may be made` `my election or revocation is made in the prescribed form and manner` `the year in which I made the election` `the year in which I revoke the election`

@export On what day does my election to exclude my income begin to have effect (s 12(1.1)(b))?
GIVEN `the date I make the election` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the election?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my election to exclude my income begin to have effect` IS
    `s 12(1.1)(b) — the first day on which the election has effect` `the date I make the election`

@export On what day does my election to exclude my income cease to have effect after I revoke it (s 12(1.1)(c))?
GIVEN `the date I revoke the election` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you revoke it?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day does my election to exclude my income cease to have effect` IS
    `s 12(1.1)(c) — the first day on which the election ceases to have effect` `the date I revoke the election`

@export Does my election to exclude my income cover this kind of income (s 12(1.1)(g))?
GIVEN `the kind of income` IS A `cp1 Kind of income an election may exclude` @desc Which kind of income are you asking about? (One of: income from a pensionable employment, self-employed earnings, another kind of income.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my election to exclude my income cover this kind of income` IF
    `s 12(1.1)(g) — an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is deemed an election in respect of the kind of income` `the kind of income`

-- s 12(1.2). If you have not revoked the election in respect of the employer, the income from that employment is not counted for sections 8 and 9.
@export How much of my pay from this employer counts for the contributions deducted from it (s 12(1.2))?
GIVEN `I have not revoked, in respect of this employer, an election in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you not revoked, in respect of this employer, an election in the prescribed form and manner?
      `my contributory salary and wages paid by this employer, as subsection 12(1) works them out` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages paid by this employer as subsection 12(1) works them out, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my pay from this employer counts for the contributions deducted from it` IS
    `s 12(1.2) — the contributory salary and wages from an employer for sections 8 and 9` `I have not revoked, in respect of this employer, an election in the prescribed form and manner` `my contributory salary and wages paid by this employer, as subsection 12(1) works them out`

-- s 12(1.2): within one year after your balance-due day (s 2(1)).
@export May I still elect under subsection 13(3) and pay my section 10 contributions on a date (s 12(1.2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person you are asking about died? (Answer yes if you are the executor or administrator of someone who has died.)
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc If the person has died, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `the date I make the election under subsection 13(3) and pay the contributions required under section 10` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the election under subsection 13(3) and pay the contributions required under section 10?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I still make the election under subsection 13(3) and pay the section 10 contributions on this date` IF
    `s 12(1.2) — the person may make an election under subsection 13(3) and pay the contributions required under section 10 on a date` `the year I am asking about` (IF `the person has died` THEN JUST `the date of death` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I make the election under subsection 13(3) and pay the contributions required under section 10`

§§ `Sections 13 to 14.1 -- my self-employed earnings`

-- s 14. Up to two businesses; a business more than half of whose gross revenue is rent, and services included in pensionable employment by regulation, are left out.
@export What are my self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars (s 14)?
GIVEN `my income for the year from my first business` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the year from my first business, as the Income Tax Act computes it, in dollars?
      `my losses sustained in the year in carrying on my first business` IS A NUMBER @desc What losses did you sustain in the year in carrying on my first business, in dollars?
      `more than half of the gross revenue of my first business was rent from land or buildings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of my first business rent from land or buildings?
      `the income or losses of my first business are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the income or losses of my first business from the performance of services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment?
      `I carry on a second business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you carry on a second business?
      `my income for the year from my second business` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the year from my second business, as the Income Tax Act computes it, in dollars?
      `my losses sustained in the year in carrying on my second business` IS A NUMBER @desc What losses did you sustain in the year in carrying on my second business, in dollars?
      `more than half of the gross revenue of my second business was rent from land or buildings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of my second business rent from land or buildings?
      `the income or losses of my second business are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the income or losses of my second business from the performance of services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment?
      `my income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an Indian as defined in the Indian Act?
      `my income for the year from self-employment on a reserve that regulations include` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your income for the year from self-employment on a reserve is not otherwise included in your income and is included by the regulations, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my self-employed earnings for the year` IS
    `s 14 — the self-employed earnings of a person for a year` (`s 14(a) — the income from businesses, less the losses sustained in carrying them on` `my businesses`) (`s 14(b) — the income from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment` `my income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment`) (`s 14(c) — the income of an Indian from self-employment on a reserve` `I am an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` `my income for the year from self-employment on a reserve that regulations include`)
    WHERE
        `my first business as a record` MEANS `cp1 Business carried on by a person` WITH
            `income of the person for the year from the business` IS `my income for the year from my first business`
            `losses sustained by the person in the year in carrying on the business` IS `my losses sustained in the year in carrying on my first business`
            `more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of the business consisted of rent from land or buildings` IS `more than half of the gross revenue of my first business was rent from land or buildings`
            `the income or losses are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment` IS `the income or losses of my first business are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment`
        `my second business as a record` MEANS `cp1 Business carried on by a person` WITH
            `income of the person for the year from the business` IS `my income for the year from my second business`
            `losses sustained by the person in the year in carrying on the business` IS `my losses sustained in the year in carrying on my second business`
            `more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of the business consisted of rent from land or buildings` IS `more than half of the gross revenue of my second business was rent from land or buildings`
            `the income or losses are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment` IS `the income or losses of my second business are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment`
        `my businesses` MEANS IF `I carry on a second business` THEN LIST `my first business as a record`, `my second business as a record` ELSE LIST `my first business as a record`

@export What part of a congregation's allocation is treated as my own business income (s 14.1)?
GIVEN `a member of my family in a congregation is specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a member of a family in a congregation specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for the year?
      `the part of the amounts allocated to the family that may reasonably be regarded as derived from a business carried on by the congregation` IS A NUMBER @desc What part of the total of all amounts allocated to the family under that subsection for the year may reasonably be regarded as derived from a business carried on by the congregation, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What part of a congregation's allocation is treated as my own business income` IS
    `s 14.1 — the income deemed to be the member's income from a business carried on by the member` `a member of my family in a congregation is specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for the year` `the part of the amounts allocated to the family that may reasonably be regarded as derived from a business carried on by the congregation`

-- s 13(1) and (2). A proportion of the self-employed earnings in a year in which you reach 18 or 70, your contributory period ends or your disability pension ceases, or an election is made or revoked;
-- nothing for a year wholly within the periods of s 12(1)(a) to (d) or after an election to exclude. NOTHING: a case the text does not apportion.
@export What are my contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars (s 13(1) and (2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your contributory period under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, end by reason of disability during the year?
      `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a disability pension payable to you under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, stop being payable during the year?
      `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any months excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
      `the first month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that run of excluded months ended?
      `the last month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If it has ended, what is the last month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `a retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to you under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month for which it is payable? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) to exclude your income after you reach sixty-five years of age?
      `the date I made that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you make it? (Any date if not.)
      `I have revoked that election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election?
      `the date I revoked that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) to exclude your self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does it refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election to exclude self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my revocation` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does the revocation refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `my self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (The question above works them out.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS
    `s 13 — the contributory self-employed earnings of a person for a year` `my facts` `my self-employed earnings for the year`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about a person for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `date of birth of the person` IS `my date of birth`
            -- Placeholder: the rules this question calls do not read the date of death.
            `date of death of the person` IS NOTHING
            `date the contributory period of the person ends by reason of disability` IS (IF `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` THEN JUST `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the disability pension ceases to be payable to the person` IS (IF `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` THEN JUST `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `months excluded from the contributory period of the person by reason of disability` IS
                IF `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` THEN LIST `my run of excluded months` ELSE EMPTY
            `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person` IS (IF `a retirement pension is payable to me` THEN JUST `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` THEN JUST `the date I made that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have revoked that election` THEN JUST `the date I revoked that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)` IS (IF `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my revocation` ELSE NOTHING)
        `my run of excluded months` MEANS `cp1 Month period` WITH
            `first month of the month period` IS `the first month excluded by reason of disability`
            `last month of the month period` IS (IF `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` THEN JUST `the last month excluded by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 13(1.1): in the prescribed form and manner (a), once for a year (b), not for a year for which an election is revoked (d), and not for a year for which you have income from pensionable employment (f).
@export May I make an election to exclude my self-employed earnings for the year (s 13(1.1))?
GIVEN `my election is made in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your election to exclude self-employed earnings made in the prescribed form and manner?
      `I have already made an election for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you already made an election to exclude self-employed earnings for the year?
      `an election of mine is revoked for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an election of yours to exclude self-employed earnings revoked for the year?
      `I have income from pensionable employment for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have income from pensionable employment for the year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I make an election to exclude my self-employed earnings for the year` IF
    `s 13(1.1) — a valid election under paragraph 13(1)(b) may be made for the year` `my election is made in the prescribed form and manner` `I have already made an election for the year` `an election of mine is revoked for the year` `I have income from pensionable employment for the year`

@export May I revoke my election to exclude my self-employed earnings for a year (s 13(1.1)(c))?
GIVEN `the year for which the election is deemed to be made` IS A NUMBER @desc For what year is your election deemed to be made?
      `the year for which I revoke the election` IS A NUMBER @desc For what year do you revoke it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I revoke my election to exclude my self-employed earnings for the year` IF
    `s 13(1.1)(c) — the election may be revoked for the year` `the year for which the election is deemed to be made` `the year for which I revoke the election`

@export On what day is my election to exclude my self-employed earnings deemed made or revoked (s 13(1.1)(e))?
GIVEN `the month my election or revocation refers to` IS A DATE @desc What month does your election or revocation refer to? (Any date in that month.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day is my election to exclude my self-employed earnings deemed made or revoked` IS
    `s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` `the month my election or revocation refers to`

-- s 13(1.2): not before the month you reach 65 (a), not before the month your retirement pension becomes payable (b), and not after the month you reach 70, counted on your actual birthday (c).
@export May my election to exclude my self-employed earnings refer to this month (s 13(1.2))?
GIVEN `the month my election or revocation refers to` IS A DATE @desc What month does your election or revocation refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the month in which my retirement pension becomes payable` IS A DATE @desc In what month does your retirement pension become payable? (Any date in that month.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my election to exclude my self-employed earnings refer to this month` IF
    `s 13(1.2) — the month referred to in the election or revocation is allowed` `the month my election or revocation refers to` `my date of birth` `the month in which my retirement pension becomes payable`

-- s 13(3): within one year from June 15 of the following year, or from the day the Minister refunds an amount under section 38. Reading taken: on or before the end of that year.
@export Is my election to include my employment earnings in my self-employed earnings made in time (s 13(3))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the date I make the election` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make the election under subsection 13(3)?
      `the Minister refunded an amount to me under section 38` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As an employee, did the Minister refund an amount to you under section 38?
      `the day on which the Minister refunded it` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my election to include my employment earnings in my self-employed earnings made in time` IF
    `s 13(3) — the election is made in time` `the year I am asking about` `the date I make the election` (IF `the Minister refunded an amount to me under section 38` THEN JUST `the day on which the Minister refunded it` ELSE NOTHING)

@export How much of my employment earnings are included in my self-employed earnings for section 10(1) if I elect (s 13(3))?
GIVEN `my contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year, in dollars?
      `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a base contribution on part of your salary and wages under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which I made that base contribution under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, on how much salary and wages (as determined in the prescribed manner), in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers and under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of your basic exemption for the year by your employers, under the Plan and under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my employment earnings are included in my self-employed earnings if I elect under subsection 13(3)` IS
    `s 13(3) — the amount included in the contributory self-employed earnings for the purposes of subsection 10(1)` `my contributory salary and wages for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` (IF `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which I made that base contribution under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING) `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers and under a provincial pension plan` `my basic exemption for the year`

@export How much of my employment earnings are included for the first additional contribution if I elect (s 13(3.1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `I or my representative make an election under subsection 13(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, or your representative, make an election under subsection 13(3)?
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year, in dollars?
      `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages for the first additional contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a first additional contribution on part of your salary and wages under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which I made that first additional contribution under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, on how much, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers and under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of your basic exemption for the year by your employers, under the Plan and under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my employment earnings are included for the first additional contribution if I elect` IS
    `s 13(3.1) — the amount included in the contributory self-employed earnings for the purposes of subsection 10(1.1)` `the year I am asking about` `I or my representative make an election under subsection 13(3)` `my contributory salary and wages for the year` `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` (IF `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages for the first additional contribution` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which I made that first additional contribution under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING) `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers and under a provincial pension plan` `my basic exemption for the year`

@export How much of my employment earnings are included for the second additional contribution if I elect (s 13(3.2))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `I or my representative make an election under subsection 13(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, or your representative, make an election under subsection 13(3)?
      `my contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year, in dollars?
      `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year, in dollars?
      `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages for the first additional contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a first additional contribution on part of your salary and wages under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which I made that first additional contribution under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, on how much, in dollars?
      `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages for the second additional contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a second additional contribution on part of your salary and wages under a provincial pension plan?
      `the salary and wages on which I made that second additional contribution under the provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, on how much, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers and under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of your basic exemption for the year by your employers, under the Plan and under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars?
      `an amount was calculated under subsection 13(3) or (3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an amount calculated for you under subsection (3) or (3.1)?
      `the amount calculated under subsection 13(3) or (3.1)` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount was calculated for you under subsection 13(3) or (3.1), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my employment earnings are included for the second additional contribution if I elect` IS
    `s 13(3.2) — the amount included in the contributory self-employed earnings for the purposes of subsection 10(1.2)` `the year I am asking about` `I or my representative make an election under subsection 13(3)` `my contributory salary and wages for the year` `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `my salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` `my salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` (IF `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages for the first additional contribution` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which I made that first additional contribution under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `a provincial pension plan counted part of that salary and wages for the second additional contribution` THEN JUST `the salary and wages on which I made that second additional contribution under the provincial pension plan` ELSE NOTHING) `all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of my basic exemption for the year by my employers and under a provincial pension plan` `my basic exemption for the year` (IF `an amount was calculated under subsection 13(3) or (3.1)` THEN JUST `the amount calculated under subsection 13(3) or (3.1)` ELSE NOTHING)

@export Which self-employed earnings count for me if I live in a province with its own plan (s 13(4))?
GIVEN `I was resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan?
      `my self-employed earnings as the provincial pension plan requires them to be computed` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your self-employed earnings for the year as the provincial pension plan requires them to be computed, in dollars?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings as this Act works them out` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory self-employed earnings as the Act works them out, in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Which contributory self-employed earnings count for me if I am resident in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS
    `s 13(4) — the contributory self-employed earnings of a person resident in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `I was resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `my self-employed earnings as the provincial pension plan requires them to be computed` `my contributory self-employed earnings as this Act works them out`

§§ `Sections 15 to 15.3 -- the salary and wages on which a contribution has been made`

-- s 15(1). The amounts of paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b) are worked out from the same facts as the excess-amount question.
-- Read literally the amount is the amount of 8(2)(a) divided by the rate, whatever was deducted (NOTES.md, finding).
@export On how much of my salary and wages has a base contribution been made for the year, in dollars (s 15(1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year from your first employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your second employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your employment to which a provincial pension plan applies (for example in Quebec), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also an individual with self-employed earnings to whom section 10 and the contribution provisions apply?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees for the year under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction? (Zero if none.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the first additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the second additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year if paragraphs 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are they if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your contributions under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your contributions under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my base contribution under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your base contribution under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my base contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your base contribution under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `On how much of my salary and wages has a base contribution been made for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the amounts determined under paragraphs (a) to (d)` `my facts`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amounts THEN
        CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST first THEN
            CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST second THEN
                `s 15(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for a year` `the contribution rate for employees for the year` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my base contribution under the Plan` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my base contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` first second
    WHERE
        `my first employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my second employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my provincial employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `my first employment`, `my second employment`, `my provincial employment`
            `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS (IF `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` THEN JUST `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS `my basic exemption for the year`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan`

-- s 15.1(1). As section 15(1), for the first additional contribution (paragraphs 8(2)(a.1) and (c)).
@export On how much of my salary and wages has a first additional contribution been made for the year, in dollars (s 15.1(1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year from your first employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your second employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your employment to which a provincial pension plan applies (for example in Quebec), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also an individual with self-employed earnings to whom section 10 and the contribution provisions apply?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees for the year under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction? (Zero if none.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the first additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the second additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year if paragraphs 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are they if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your contributions under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your contributions under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my first additional contribution under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your first additional contribution under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my first additional contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your first additional contribution under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `On how much of my salary and wages has a first additional contribution been made for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the amounts determined under paragraphs (a) to (d)` `my facts`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amounts THEN
        CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)`)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST first THEN
            CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)`)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST second THEN
                `s 15.1(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for a year` `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my first additional contribution under the Plan` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my first additional contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` first second
    WHERE
        `my first employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my second employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my provincial employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `my first employment`, `my second employment`, `my provincial employment`
            `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS (IF `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` THEN JUST `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS `my basic exemption for the year`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan`

-- s 15.2(1). "The amount determined under subsection 8(2)" is read as the excess amount calculated (NOTES.md, fork register).
@export On how much of my salary and wages has a second additional contribution been made for the year, in dollars (s 15.2(1))?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your contributory salary and wages for the year from your first employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars?
      `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your second employment to which the Plan applies, in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And from your employment to which a provincial pension plan applies (for example in Quebec), in dollars? (Zero if none.)
      `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also an individual with self-employed earnings to whom section 10 and the contribution provisions apply?
      `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what are your contributory self-employed earnings for the year, in dollars? (Zero if not.)
      `the contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.0495 for 4.95%)? (It is set out in Schedule 1; the question on section 11.1 gives it.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.01 for 1%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year, as a fraction (for example 0.04 for 4%)? (Schedule 2.)
      `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the base contribution rate for employees for the year under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction? (Zero if none.)
      `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the first additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the second additional rate under the provincial pension plan, as a fraction?
      `my basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year, in dollars? (Section 19.)
      `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your basic exemption for the year if paragraphs 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum contributory earnings for the year, in dollars?
      `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are they if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c) (the elections) are left out, in dollars?
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.)
      `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 17.1.)
      `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS A NUMBER @desc What are your additional maximum pensionable earnings if paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c) are left out, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year, by all your employers, on account of your contributions under the Plan, in dollars?
      `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your contributions under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my base contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your base contribution under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my first additional contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc And the total deducted on account of your first additional contribution under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
      `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my second additional contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts deducted from your remuneration for the year on account of your second additional contribution under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `On how much of my salary and wages has a second additional contribution been made for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the amounts determined under paragraphs (a) to (d)` `my facts`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST amounts THEN
        CONSIDER `s 8(8) — the ratio of the salary and wages under this Act to the aggregate, each employment limited by the additional maximum pensionable earnings` `my facts`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST ratio THEN
            CONSIDER `s 8(2) — the excess amount calculated` `my facts`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST excess THEN
                CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a)`)
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST a THEN
                    CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(b)`)
                    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                    WHEN JUST b THEN
                        CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(a.1)`)
                        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                        WHEN JUST a1 THEN
                            CONSIDER (amounts's `amount determined under paragraph 8(2)(c)`)
                            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                            WHEN JUST c THEN
                                `s 15.2(1) — the amount of a person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for a year` ratio `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my second additional contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` (`s 15(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a) and (b)` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my base contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` a b) (`s 15.1(1)(b)(ii)(B) — the aggregate deducted under this Act or a provincial pension plan, minus the sum of the amounts determined under paragraphs 8(2)(a.1) and (c)` `all amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year on account of my first additional contribution under the Plan or a provincial pension plan` a1 c) excess
    WHERE
        `my first employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my first employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my second employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my second employment under the Plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS TRUE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS FALSE
        `my provincial employment` MEANS `cp1 Employment of an employee in a year` WITH
            `contributory salary and wages of the employee from the employment` IS `my contributory salary and wages from my employment under a provincial pension plan`
            `the provisions of this Act relating to the making of contributions apply to the employment` IS FALSE
            `the provisions of a provincial pension plan apply to the employment` IS TRUE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about the contributions of an employee for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `employments of the employee in the year` IS LIST `my first employment`, `my second employment`, `my provincial employment`
            `contributory self-employed earnings of the employee for the year, if the employee is an individual described in section 10 to whom the provisions relating to the making of contributions apply` IS (IF `I am an individual described in section 10 to whom the contribution provisions apply` THEN JUST `my contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE NOTHING)
            `the contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under this Act` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year`
            `the base contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the base contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the first additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the first additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the second additional contribution rate for employees for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS `the second additional contribution rate for employees under a provincial pension plan`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year` IS `my basic exemption for the year`
            `the employee's basic exemption for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 19(b) and (c)` IS `my basic exemption for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum contributory earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum contributory earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c) and 19(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17(b) and (c)` IS `my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17(b) and (c)`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
            `the employee's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, determined without taking into account paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)` IS `my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, leaving out the effect of paragraphs 17.1(b) and (c)`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan`
            `aggregate of all amounts deducted as required from the remuneration of the employee for the year on account of the employee's contributions under this Act or under a provincial pension plan` IS `all the amounts deducted from my remuneration for the year as my contributions under the Plan or a provincial pension plan`

-- If your employer failed to deduct an amount as required and you notified the Minister before June 30 of the following year, the amount that should have been deducted is added to the aggregate deducted.
@export If my employer failed to deduct, is the amount added when I tell the Minister in time (s 15(1.1), 15.1(1.1) and 15.2(1.1))?
GIVEN `the contribution I am asking about is` IS A Tier @desc Which contribution are you asking about? (One of: the base tier, the first additional tier, the second additional tier.)
      `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to deduct an amount as required from your remuneration on account of that contribution for the year?
      `the amount my employer should have deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount should your employer have deducted on account of that contribution, in dollars?
      `I notified the Minister of my employer's failure to deduct that amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Minister of your employer's failure to deduct that amount?
      `the date I notified the Minister` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Is the amount my employer failed to deduct added to what was deducted because I told the Minister in time` IS
    CONSIDER `the contribution I am asking about is`
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `s 15(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the base contribution` `the year I am asking about` `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` `the amount my employer should have deducted` (IF `I notified the Minister of my employer's failure to deduct that amount` THEN JUST `the date I notified the Minister` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN `s 15.1(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the first additional contribution` `the year I am asking about` `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` `the amount my employer should have deducted` (IF `I notified the Minister of my employer's failure to deduct that amount` THEN JUST `the date I notified the Minister` ELSE NOTHING)
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN `s 15.2(1.1) — the amount added to the aggregate of the amounts deducted on account of the second additional contribution` `the year I am asking about` `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` `the amount my employer should have deducted` (IF `I notified the Minister of my employer's failure to deduct that amount` THEN JUST `the date I notified the Minister` ELSE NOTHING)

@export If my employer paid an amount it failed to deduct, is it treated as deducted from my pay (s 15(2), 15.1(2) and 15.2(2))?
GIVEN `the contribution I am asking about is` IS A Tier @desc Which contribution are you asking about? (One of: the base tier, the first additional tier, the second additional tier.)
      `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employer fail to deduct an amount as required from your remuneration on account of that contribution for the year?
      `the amount my employer paid on account of that contribution` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount did your employer pay on account of that contribution for the year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Is an amount my employer paid after failing to deduct it treated as deducted from my pay` IS
    CONSIDER `the contribution I am asking about is`
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN `s 15(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the base contribution` `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` `the amount my employer paid on account of that contribution`
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN `s 15.1(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the first additional contribution` `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` `the amount my employer paid on account of that contribution`
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN `s 15.2(2) — the amount deemed to have been deducted by the employer on account of the second additional contribution` `my employer failed to deduct an amount as required from my remuneration on account of that contribution` `the amount my employer paid on account of that contribution`

@export May the amount shown in my employer's return be used in place of the amounts deducted (s 15.3)?
GIVEN `my employer has filed a return showing an amount as the salary and wages on which contributions have been made by me for the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your employer filed a return in accordance with Part I showing an amount as the salary and wages on which contributions have been made by you for the year?
      `the amount shown in that return` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount does the return show, in dollars?
      `the rate for employees for the year for that contribution` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the contribution rate, the first additional rate or the second additional rate, as the case may be, for employees for the year, as a fraction?
      `the circumstances are prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances prescribed by regulation?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `May the amount shown in my employer's return be used in place of the amounts deducted` IS
    `s 15.3 — the amount that may be substituted for the aggregate of the amounts deducted by the employer` `my employer has filed a return showing an amount as the salary and wages on which contributions have been made by me for the year` `the amount shown in that return` `the rate for employees for the year for that contribution` `the circumstances are prescribed`

§§ `Sections 16 to 20 -- the maximums and the basic exemption`

-- s 18. 25,900 for 1987; from 1988 the preceding year's amount times the ratio of two twelve-month averages of the Wage Measure (figures Statistics Canada publishes; the Act does not contain them),
-- rounded down to a multiple of 100 but never below the preceding year's amount. NOTHING: before 1987, or an average of nil.
@export What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year, in dollars (s 18)?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections 18(2) and (3)` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections (2) and (3), in dollars?
      `the average Wage Measure for the twelve months ending June 30 of the preceding year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the average of the Wage Measure for each month in the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the preceding year?
      `the average Wage Measure for the twelve months ending June 30 of the year before that` IS A NUMBER @desc And for the twelve month period ending on June 30 of the year immediately preceding the preceding year?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year` IS A NUMBER @desc What was the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year` IS
    CONSIDER `s 18(1) — the amount calculated for a year` `the year I am asking about` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year, calculated without reference to subsections 18(2) and (3)` `the average Wage Measure for the twelve months ending June 30 of the preceding year` `the average Wage Measure for the twelve months ending June 30 of the year before that`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST calculated THEN `s 18 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the year I am asking about` calculated `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the preceding year`

-- s 18.1. For 2024, 1.07 times the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings; for 2025 and later, 1.14 times; rounded down to a multiple of 100.
@export What is the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year, in dollars (s 18.1)?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 18; the question above works it out.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year` IS
    `s 18.1 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the year I am asking about` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year`

-- s 20. 3,500 dollars for each year after 1997; before that, the highest multiple of 100 dollars not above 10% of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings. NOTHING: before 1987.
@export What is the Year's Basic Exemption for the year, in dollars (s 20)?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 18; the question above works it out.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the Year's Basic Exemption for the year` IS
    `s 20 — the Year's Basic Exemption` `the year I am asking about` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year`

-- s 17. The Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, prorated by months in a year in which you reach 18 or 70, die, your contributory period ends or your disability pension ceases (a), or an election is made (b) or revoked (c).
-- NOTHING: two election events in one year.
@export What are my maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars (s 17)?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person you are asking about died? (Answer yes if you are the executor or administrator of someone who has died.)
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc If the person has died, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your contributory period under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, end by reason of disability during the year?
      `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a disability pension payable to you under the Plan, or under a provincial pension plan, stop being payable during the year?
      `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any months excluded from your contributory period by reason of disability?
      `the first month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that run of excluded months ended?
      `the last month excluded by reason of disability` IS A DATE @desc If it has ended, what is the last month excluded? (Any date in that month.)
      `a retirement pension is payable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a retirement pension payable to you under the Plan or under a provincial pension plan?
      `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the first month for which it is payable? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) to exclude your income after you reach sixty-five years of age?
      `the date I made that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date did you make it? (Any date if not.)
      `I have revoked that election` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election?
      `the date I revoked that election` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Any date if not.)
      `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) to exclude your self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does it refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you revoked that election to exclude self-employed earnings?
      `the month referred to in my revocation` IS A DATE @desc If so, what month does the revocation refer to? (Any date in that month.)
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year, in dollars? (Section 18; the question above works it out.)
      `leave out the effect of my elections (paragraphs (b) and (c))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you want the figure with the effect of your elections (paragraphs (b) and (c)) left out, as subsections 8(6), (7), (10) and (11) ask for?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What are my maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS
    IF `leave out the effect of my elections (paragraphs (b) and (c))`
    THEN `s 17 — the maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year, determined without taking into account paragraphs (b) and (c)` `my facts` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year`
    ELSE `s 17 — the maximum pensionable earnings of a person for a year` `my facts` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `cp1 Facts about a person for a year` WITH
            `the year at hand` IS `the year I am asking about`
            `date of birth of the person` IS `my date of birth`
            `date of death of the person` IS (IF `the person has died` THEN JUST `the date of death` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the contributory period of the person ends by reason of disability` IS (IF `my contributory period ended by reason of disability in the year` THEN JUST `the date my contributory period ended by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the disability pension ceases to be payable to the person` IS (IF `my disability pension stopped being payable in the year` THEN JUST `the date my disability pension stopped being payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `months excluded from the contributory period of the person by reason of disability` IS
                IF `some months are excluded from my contributory period by reason of disability` THEN LIST `my run of excluded months` ELSE EMPTY
            `month from which a retirement pension is payable to the person` IS (IF `a retirement pension is payable to me` THEN JUST `the first month for which my retirement pension is payable` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my income after I reach sixty-five` THEN JUST `the date I made that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)` IS (IF `I have revoked that election` THEN JUST `the date I revoked that election` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)` IS (IF `I have made an election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` ELSE NOTHING)
            `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)` IS (IF `I have revoked my election to exclude my self-employed earnings` THEN JUST `the month referred to in my revocation` ELSE NOTHING)
        `my run of excluded months` MEANS `cp1 Month period` WITH
            `first month of the month period` IS `the first month excluded by reason of disability`
            `last month of the month period` IS (IF `the months excluded by reason of disability have ended` THEN JUST `the last month excluded by reason of disability` ELSE NOTHING)

-- s 17.1. As section 17, with the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings.
@export What are my additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year, in dollars (s 17.1)?
GIVEN `the year I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc Which calendar year are you asking about?
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc What is your date of birth?
      `the person has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person you are asking about died? (Answer yes if you are the executor or administrator of someone who has died.)
      `the date of death` IS A DATE @desc If the person has died, on what date? (Any date if not.)
